//! to a shared queue in the Amazon SQS Developer Guide.
//!
//! ## Input
//!
//! * `QueueName` (String) **required** — (Required) The name of the queue for which you want
//!   to fetch the URL. The name can be up to 80 characters long and can include alphanumeric
//!   characters, hyphens (-), and underscores (_). Queue URLs and names are case-sensitive.
//! * `QueueOwnerAWSAccountId` (String) — (Optional) The Amazon Web Services account ID of the
//!   account that created the queue. This is only required when you are attempting to access
//!   a queue owned by another Amazon Web Services account.
//!
//! ## Output
//!
//! * `QueueUrl` (String) — The URL of the queue.
//!
//! ## Errors
//!
//! * `InvalidAddress` (HTTP 404) — The specified ID is invalid.
//! * `InvalidSecurity` (HTTP 403) — The request was not made over HTTPS or did not use SigV4
//!   for signing.
//! * `QueueDoesNotExist` (HTTP 400) — Ensure that the QueueUrl is correct and that the queue
//!   has not been deleted.
